  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math> { <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is not a positive integer} <math><mo>.</mo></math> Define a function <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> as <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , then <math><mi>f</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Injective but not surjective",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Not injective",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Surjective but not injective",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither injective nor surjective",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, function <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and domain of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi></math> is always decreasing in the given domain.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0166_ca4b9daf05a0.png\" /><br /><br />Clearly, given function is one-one or injective.<br />Since, codomain <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo></math> Range <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> , hence <math><mi>f</mi></math> is into.</p>"
